    "english": "In Korean folk culture, the mole carries multiple layers of symbolic meaning. First, as an underground creature, it represents hidden things, invisible truths, and subterranean labor. The mole's tireless digging came to symbolize quiet, persistent effort in an agrarian society, giving rise to the expression 'a farmer is a mole.' Second, the most important folk narrative attached to the mole is the '두더지 혼인 설화' (Mole's Marriage Tale). In this story, a mole seeks the greatest son-in-law in the world, visiting Heaven, the Sun, clouds, wind, and a stone Buddha in turn, only to be told by the stone Buddha that the mole itself — able to burrow beneath all things — is the most powerful. The mole returns home and chooses another mole as a spouse. This tale cautions against vain ambitions and excessive pride that exceed one's station, and the proverb '두더지 혼인같다' (like a mole's marriage) is used to describe futile pursuits of prestige beyond one's means. Mole dreams therefore can carry a message to reflect on one's true worth and proper place. Third, because moles have extremely poor eyesight and avoid light, the animal also symbolizes a person who cannot see reality clearly or who is trapped in their own isolated world."
  },
  "westernContext": {
    "freudian": {
      "korean": "프로이트의 관점에서 두더지와 땅을 파는 행위는 억압된 무의식의 내용이 의식의 표면으로 밀려 올라오려는 충동을 상징합니다. 두더지가 지하에서 지상으로 나오는 꿈은 억눌려 있던 욕망, 기억, 또는 갈등이 의식화되는 과정을 나타낼 수 있으며, 두더지 구멍은 여성적 원리나 무의식으로의 통로를 상징하기도 합니다.",
      "english": "From a Freudian perspective, the mole and its digging represent the urge of repressed unconscious content to push its way toward conscious awareness. A mole emerging from underground may symbolize the process of suppressed desires, memories, or conflicts becoming conscious. Mole holes can represent the feminine principle or a passage into the unconscious."
    },
    "jungian": {
      "korean": "융의 분석심리학에서 두더지는 지하 세계의 거주자로서 심층 무의식, 즉 집단 무의식의 가장 깊은 층을 상징합니다. 두더지 꿈은 자아가 아직 통합하지 못한 그림자(Shadow) 원형과의 만남을 나타낼 수 있습니다. 두더지가 땅을 파는 행위는 자기 자신의 내면 깊이를 탐색하고 개성화(individuation)의 여정을 진행하는 것을 상징합니다. 두더지의 작은 체구와 강한 굴착 능력은 외면적으로는 미약해 보이지만 내적으로 강한 힘을 가진 개인의 심리 상태를 반영하기도 합니다.",
      "english": "In Jungian analytical psychology, the mole as an underground dweller symbolizes the deep unconscious, specifically the deepest layers of the collective unconscious. A mole dream may represent an encounter with the Shadow archetype — aspects of the self not yet integrated into conscious awareness. The act of digging symbolizes the process of exploring one's inner depths and advancing along the journey of individuation. The mole's small body paired with powerful digging ability may also reflect a psychological state of hidden inner strength beneath an unassuming exterior."
