      "english": "From a modern psychological perspective, mole dreams are commonly linked to problems the dreamer is facing but reluctant to confront directly. The mole's poor eyesight symbolizes reality avoidance or selective perception. The act of digging may represent an unconscious drive to address problems at their root. If mole dreams occur frequently during periods of high stress, they may signal the accumulation of unresolved conflicts or anxieties in the inner world."
    },
    "crossCultural": {
      "korean": "동서양을 막론하고 두더지는 '숨겨진 것'과 '지하 세계'의 상징으로 공통적으로 인식됩니다. 서양에서 두더지는 '두더지 잡기(Whack-a-Mole)' 게임으로 대표되듯 끊임없이 재발하는 문제를 상징하기도 하고, 영어 표현 'make a mountain out of a molehill(두더지 둔덕으로 산을 만들다)'은 사소한 일을 과장하는 태도를 비유합니다. 일본 민속에서도 두더지는 땅 속의 풍요와 관련되며, 인도 우화에서는 '두더지 혼인 설화'와 유사한 이야기가 전해지는 등 아시아 전반에 걸쳐 분수에 맞게 사는 삶의 지혜를 가르치는 존재로 등장합니다.",
      "english": "Across cultures, the mole is universally recognized as a symbol of hidden things and the underworld. In Western culture, moles are associated with endlessly recurring problems (as in the Whack-a-Mole game), and the expression 'make a mountain out of a molehill' describes the tendency to exaggerate trivial matters. In Japanese folklore, moles are connected to underground abundance. In Indian fables, a story nearly identical to Korea's '두더지 혼인 설화' is found, confirming that across Asia, the mole serves as a teacher of the wisdom of living within one's proper place."
    }
  },
